Follow-up push: the option now reads an environment variable holding the whole list.

A prototyped list refuses a whole `%env()%` value, whatever type the processor declares for it, because `ArrayNode::allowPlaceholders()` is false and the type map is never consulted:

```
plain prototyped list + %env(X)%       => A dynamic value is not compatible with a "PrototypedArrayNode" node type
plain prototyped list + %env(json:X)%  => A dynamic value is not compatible with a "PrototypedArrayNode" node type
```

`acceptAndWrap()` gets around that by wrapping the placeholder into a one-element list before the type check, which is what made `%env(AUD)%` work here. It is also what silently nested `%env(json:AUDS)%` into `[["a","b"]]`.

So the bundle unwraps it again on the way out, which is what `FrameworkExtension` already does for `trusted_hosts` and `trusted_proxies`:

```php
$audience = [0] === array_keys($config['audience']) ? $config['audience'][0] : $config['audience'];
```

Together with the `string|list<string>` argument this PR adds, the environment variable decides the shape. Measured through the real factories, from the config node to the resolved container argument:

```
oidc,   a string             => "https://api.example.com"
oidc,   a list               => ["https://api.example.com","https://admin.example.com"]
oidc,   %env(AUD)%           => "https://api.example.com"
oidc,   %env(json:AUDS)%     => ["https://api.example.com","https://admin.example.com"]
oauth2, %env(json:AUDS)%     => ["https://api.example.com","https://admin.example.com"]
oauth2, no audience          => []
```

`Oauth2TokenHandler` takes the same `string|list<string>` argument for its half, and validates its entries the way the oidc handler does, so an empty string no longer builds a handler that refuses every token.

A side effect worth naming: the container argument keeps the plain string it had when a single identifier is configured, so the six expectations this PR was changing from `'audience'` to `['audience']` are back to what they were. The only fixture that moves is the one oauth2 test where a lone audience is now passed as a string.

Security/Http `OK (1188 tests, 2681 assertions)`, SecurityBundle `OK (631, 1759)`.
